nd viewer fingerprints), corresponding to TestADepartedRequesterCannotRatifyAReviewApproval. The regression must fail against the unrepaired authority.ts. (2) The cache witness proves the transition this head actually makes: TestAnOlderProfileCacheIsRebuiltUnderTheNewRules is re-anchored to oldProfile @12, seeds a cached statement with Satisfier removed and its admitted value known, and asserts that replay under @13 restores that exact value and replaces the profile; the comments describe @12 to @13. Keep the older receipt witness only as a separate test that still earns its weight. (3) The gates codex ran at 477637589 pass at the new head with -count=1: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -count=1 ./..., gofmt -l empty, npm test --prefix ui, make ui-check, git diff --check, and the post-build internal/service/uidist byte comparison. (4) Nothing else changes. The receipt-checkpoint behaviour carried in base 10c6d623 is out of scope; it has its own approved and ratified exact-head review and must not be re-litigated here.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}